## `--explain`: a grant, a denial, and the direction

Inclusion by zenoh-keyexpr, per direction, with the rules that decided. The
console asking a write procedure: `no-remote-actions` beats `ops-sub`.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment.toml --format table --explain zensight-console 'zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/@rpc/systemd/action/set' query
no registry asked: the planes are as the enrollment claims, and no-remote-actions denies the convention's write leaf zensight/v1/*/@rpc/*/**/set rather than the declared write procedures — pass --registry <dir> to narrow both to what the fleet actually declares (RFC 13 §3 O4)
zensight-console  query  zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/@rpc/systemd/action/set
  ingress  DENIED  no-remote-actions denies query on ingress — deny wins over ops-sub
      ✗ no-remote-actions  deny  zensight/v1/*/@rpc/*/**/set
      ✓ ops-sub  allow  zensight/v1/*/@rpc/**
  egress   DENIED  no-remote-actions denies query on egress — deny wins
      ✗ no-remote-actions  deny  zensight/v1/*/@rpc/*/**/set

```

A host publishing its own state: allowed on ingress, and nothing on egress
— which is right, a put never leaves the router toward its own author.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment.toml --format table --explain h-3fa9c2d41b7e 'zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/state/sysinfo/health' put
no registry asked: the planes are as the enrollment claims, and no-remote-actions denies the convention's write leaf zensight/v1/*/@rpc/*/**/set rather than the declared write procedures — pass --registry <dir> to narrow both to what the fleet actually declares (RFC 13 §3 O4)
h-3fa9c2d41b7e  put  zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/state/sysinfo/health
  ingress  ALLOWED            host-data-h-3fa9c2d41b7e includes it for put on ingress
      ✓ host-data-h-3fa9c2d41b7e  allow  zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/**
  egress   denied by default  no rule of h-3fa9c2d41b7e's policies includes zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/state/sysinfo/health for put on egress: default_permission deny

```

The same host on another host's origin — denied by default, no rule
includes it — and its own `@rpc` reply, which `host-data`'s `**` does not
reach and `host-serve` does (fact 1).

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment.toml --format table --explain h-3fa9c2d41b7e 'zensight/v1/h-0123456789ab/state/sysinfo/health' put
no registry asked: the planes are as the enrollment claims, and no-remote-actions denies the convention's write leaf zensight/v1/*/@rpc/*/**/set rather than the declared write procedures — pass --registry <dir> to narrow both to what the fleet actually declares (RFC 13 §3 O4)
h-3fa9c2d41b7e  put  zensight/v1/h-0123456789ab/state/sysinfo/health
  ingress  denied by default  no rule of h-3fa9c2d41b7e's policies includes zensight/v1/h-0123456789ab/state/sysinfo/health for put on ingress: default_permission deny
  egress   denied by default  no rule of h-3fa9c2d41b7e's policies includes zensight/v1/h-0123456789ab/state/sysinfo/health for put on egress: default_permission deny

```

